>Finally, I have a question about altars.  I've figured out you can 
>sacrifice corpses there.  (I'm assuming #offer is the same as 
>sacrifice.)  

Yes.

>However, sacrificing doesn't seem to accomplish anything. 
>People say you should... and whenever I'm on a level with an altar of 
>the correct alignment, I haul over corpses of things and #offer them 
>up... they disappear in a burst of flame (or nothing happens and I still 
>have the corpse.)  

Two issues here. "Nothing happens": Your gods like only fresh corpses.
You know that corpses which are too old should not be eaten? It's the
same with offerings. Additionally, you will not get spectacular effects
for /each/ offering. Keep attention to the various messages you might
receive after #offering. And be assured that repeated offerings will
eventually lead to some good results.

